      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-21T16:17:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have a bunch of these constants in each interface. Since we can\u0027t define constants in HIDL, it does make sense to group them together under \"Constants\"? I can use \"FieldSizes\" here, but it\u0027ll still remain \"Constants\" in the other interfaces.",
      "parentUuid": "70d83709_fe2d7a02",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "4fdc07ca388482d26679d10104b19a070799b25c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70d83709_9eb6ae8f",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicantNetwork.hal",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 20,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-21T17:03:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s better to just break up these constants into enums representing semantic groups. If you used c2hal to convert your HAL, it creates enums of Constants out of necessity, not because it makes a good interface.",
