    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70d83709_1e363e3d",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicantNetworkCallback.hal",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-21T16:14:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are a lot of possibile combinations. wpa_supplicant likes passing string commands around :). \nBut, in android we only use a subset of these. Maybe we can come up with a enum for those. This will require some digging around. Will follow up in a separate CL if this can be changed. Filed b/31646740 to track this.",
      "parentUuid": "70d83709_d0351531",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "4fdc07ca388482d26679d10104b19a070799b25c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70d83709_be2db2a1",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/ISupplicantNetworkCallback.hal",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-21T17:03:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Digging around is okay. If you can make this an enum, I would prefer you to go ahead and create one now, even if you only know a subset of the possibilities. This is important as each command defines a part of the interface. With the string, part of this interface is defined elsewhere. Thus, the interface can be modified without affecting hidl versioning.\n\nWe can talk about this offline more if you want.",
      "parentUuid": "70d83709_1e363e3d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 51,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "4fdc07ca388482d26679d10104b19a070799b25c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
